  "facts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Big Lake is the largest oxbow lake in Missouri, formed when the Missouri River changed course and left a 646‑acre loop behind.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Lake%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The lake’s 646‑acre basin was created as the river’s meandering loops filled with sediment, turning the standing water into an oxbow lake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Lake%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Historic floods in 1903, 1920, and 1929 repeatedly reshaped Big Lake’s shoreline, prompting community rebuilding efforts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.biglakeimprovementassociation.com/big-lake-history"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1956 residents united to form the Big Lake Improvement Association, a group dedicated to preserving the lake’s natural beauty.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.biglakeimprovementassociation.com/big-lake-history"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The first written account of Big Lake comes from the Lewis & Clark expedition, which charted the Louisiana Purchase in the early 1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.biglakeimprovementassociation.com/big-lake-history"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "When Europeans first arrived in northwest Missouri, they found a maze of wetlands and lakes teeming with fish and waterfowl, including Big Lake.",
